/*
Ported from dfinity/motoko test/run-drun/idl-nat-int.mo.
Each //CALL is an assert at the method's parameter types (Motoko -> Candid:
Nat nat, Int int, Text text, Char nat32, Float float64, Any reserved, None empty,
Null null, ?T opt T, [T] vec T, (T, U) record { T; U } or an argument list,
{#a : T} variant { a : T }, actor {..} service {..}, shared .. -> async .. func).
A trap (IDL error) is !:, a reply is : (with the decoded value where useful).
*/
assert blob "DIDL\00\01\7d\2a" == "(42)" : (int) "idl-nat-int.mo absolute: nat at int";
assert blob "DIDL\00\01\7c\56" == "(-42)" : (int) "idl-nat-int.mo absolute: int";
assert blob "DIDL\01\6d\7d\01\00\02\2a\19" == "(vec { 42; 25 })" : (vec int) "idl-nat-int.mo absolutes: vec nat at vec int";
assert blob "DIDL\01\6d\7c\01\00\02\56\19" == "(vec { -42; 25 })" : (vec int) "idl-nat-int.mo absolutes: vec int";
